From f5648ea9bf4090b03cdb91b20a37626d28a51cbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:49:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Far spaces: typed far data, translated at each access (WIP)

#pragma farspace(n, tag, ...) puts struct types in far space n, and
#pragma farsection(section, n) puts a section's objects there. The
front end tags each load, store and copy with the space of the memory
it reaches. A late pass, after every pass that moves instructions,
puts t = FARXLAT(address) right before each far access and makes the
access go through t. Native code calls the program's farxlN routine
with the page in X, which returns the RAM page in A.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
